															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/glewmie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3448977); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3448977&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200924" alt="glewmie" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3448977)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/glewmie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3448977); return false;" >glewmie</a></span> <span class="odate time_1574189327 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Nov 2019 18:48</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4427217">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Workers will not leave SCP-4651 <strong>voluntary</strong> and will vanish if forcible extraction is attempted, re-emerging the next day.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>Voluntary</em> is an adjective.<br />
&quot;Your voluntary participation is appreciated.&quot;</p>
<p><em>Voluntarily</em> is an adverb.<br />
&quot;They participated voluntarily.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Furthermore, workers <strong>have proven unable</strong> to recall details of a life beyond their employment, instead placing extreme value on their standing within the company.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'have proven' vs. 'have been proven'</p>
<p>&quot;The lab boys have proven that the rations are nutritionally complete.&quot;<br />
The lab boys are doing the proving. They proved a fact about the rations.</p>
<p>&quot;The rations have been proven to actually not be nutritionally complete.&quot;<br />
A fact about the rations has been proven.</p>
<p>Right now, your sentence reads like the workers are doing the proving, but you probably mean that the research is proving something.</p>
<p>Beyond that, it was a fun, short read. Thank you for sharing.</p>

							</div>

								
					
